    "created_at": "2016-08-22T06:05:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-22T06:05:51Z",
    "body": "When the opaque response is compressed, and the `Content-Length` header is present, it's possible to launch a compression-based attack (described in more detail [here](https://tom.vg/2016/08/request-and-conquer/#compression-based-attacks)) with this size-exposing attack. Similar to https://github.com/w3c/resource-timing/issues/64, this allows an attacker to leak content from cross-origin resources.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
